Cell["\<\
The trick here is that using With[ ], we do not need Evaluate[ ].  Now we are \
ready to define a function to draw the image of a set of parallel lines:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Curves[expr_, \ spread_, \ bounds_]\  := \ 
      With[{cvs\  = \ 
            Table[\ {Re[expr], \ Im[expr]}, \ 
              spread]}, \[IndentingNewLine]ParametricPlot[cvs, \ 
          bounds]\[IndentingNewLine]]\)], "Input"],

Cell["\<\
Note that expr must be an expression in terms of x and y, e.g. Sin[x + I y].  \
The spread specifies how many lines to draws, and bounds specify the limits \
of the lines.  This function works both for horizontal lines as well as \
vertical lines.  E.g.:\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(Curves[
      Sin[x\  + \ I\ y], \ {y, \ 0.0, \ 1.0, \ 0.2}, \ {x, \ 0.0, \ 
        1.0}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[GraphicsData["PostScript", "\<\
